Nginx Container Deployment on Application Server 3
Project Overview
As part of the Nautilus DevOps application deployment testing phase, an isolated Nginx web container must be successfully deployed, configured, and maintained in a running state on Application Server 3 (stapp03).

Infrastructure Specifications
Server Name	Hostname	User	Purpose
Jump Host Server	jump-host	thor	Secure gateway access
Application Server 3	stapp03	banner	Hosts Nautilus Application 3 component
Deployment Instructions
1. Access Application Server 3
Establish an SSH connection from the jump host to Application Server 3 using the designated user credentials (banner):

Bash
ssh banner@stapp03
Password: BigGr33n

2. Run the Nginx Alpine Container
Deploy the container with the nginx_3 name using the lightweight Alpine-tagged image in detached mode:

Bash
docker run -d --name nginx_3 nginx:alpine
3. Verify Container Status
Check the Docker container process list to ensure that nginx_3 is up and running correctly:

Bash
docker ps --filter name=nginx_3
